{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544666-can-vampires-embrace-animals","id":1544666,"title":"Can vampires embrace animals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-24T12:02:15-07:00","id":1544666,"title":"Can vampires embrace animals?","content":"I remember reading in the Vampire: the Dark Ages book that Gargoyles can embrace animals and I heard that Setites can embrace animals as well. Is this just a 1st edition thing or is it still canon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 10-24-2024, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T12:07:40-07:00","id":1544667,"title":"","content":"I can't remember the source right now, but you're right about the Setites. Probably non-canon by now (although I personally subscribe to the idea that if it was published it's fair game as a form of canon), but they found a way to embrace snakes and use them as temple guards or something. It probably requires blood sorcery of some kind.<br /> <br /> Edit: Aabbt kindred from Berlin By Night. There's only 15 of them and they're the unique creation of a 4th gen ancient, so it's definitely not a normal thing but it can be done in exceptional cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 10-24-2024, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T13:10:35-07:00","id":1544674,"title":"","content":"You shouldn't, but Berlin by Night we had a Follower of Set with two serpents that were considered embraced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T13:30:25-07:00","id":1544677,"title":"","content":"The FAQ section of White Wolf's website explicitly states 'no' in the Revised edition. Vampirism is a curse directed specifically at humans, not other animals. And honestly the very concept of vampire Chihuahuas, parrots, or goldfish destroys any sense of horror or dark fantasy, leaving only farce in its wake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T13:37:09-07:00","id":1544679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544666-can-vampires-embrace-animals?p=1544677#post1544677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The FAQ section of White Wolf's website explicitly states 'no' in the Revised edition. Vampirism is a curse directed specifically at humans, not other animals. And honestly the very concept of vampire Chihuahuas, parrots, or goldfish destroys any sense of horror or dark fantasy, leaving only farce in its wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is completely legitimate to shove a Bane into any of the above animals to create a Fomori to terrorize and occasionally tenderize the PCs. Though to be fair with Nosferatu vitae you can also mutate and enhance animals as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T13:40:03-07:00","id":1544680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544666-can-vampires-embrace-animals?p=1544677#post1544677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The FAQ section of White Wolf's website explicitly states 'no' in the Revised edition. Vampirism is a curse directed specifically at humans, not other animals. And honestly the very concept of vampire Chihuahuas, parrots, or goldfish destroys any sense of horror or dark fantasy, leaving only farce in its wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can do it with Ghouls. So, my headcanon would be that only certain rituals can turn animals into vampire creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T14:06:47-07:00","id":1544681,"title":"","content":"Vampire-like, maybe. Just keep in mind that any such creature has no way to resist the Beast, and in most cases, may even lack the instinctual understanding to seek shelter from the sun before falling unconscious at the end of the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T17:53:38-07:00","id":1544693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544666-can-vampires-embrace-animals#post1544666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember reading in the Vampire: the Dark Ages book that Gargoyles can embrace animals and I heard that Setites can embrace animals as well. Is this just a 1st edition thing or is it still canon?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was canon but has been retconned. The idea is kind of goofy. You can get something close enough with ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T18:06:44-07:00","id":1544695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544666-can-vampires-embrace-animals?p=1544693#post1544693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was canon but has been retconned. The idea is kind of goofy. You can get something close enough with ghouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answered. Just to complement, you needed animalism 6 to remove the Beast of the animal, otherwise it would just go insta frenzy, until cooking under the Sun.<br /> <br /> That was actually one of the few cases of a good retcon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T21:36:14-07:00","id":1544706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1544666-can-vampires-embrace-animals?p=1544677#post1544677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The FAQ section of White Wolf's website explicitly states 'no' in the Revised edition. Vampirism is a curse directed specifically at humans, not other animals. And honestly the very concept of vampire Chihuahuas, parrots, or goldfish destroys any sense of horror or dark fantasy, leaving only farce in its wake.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, humans themselves are kind of derpy in terms of physical presence, and don't tend to be able to flay sheep the way that kea parrots could without using a sharp object (possibly having to knap or forge one first), so I would consider the sense of horror kind of ruined from the start, for the entire game. You want me to take the frailest great ape seriously because you added a set of modest fangs?<br /> <br /> &quot;So you have the power of cursed blood on your side? Well, maybe you'll be able to fight a chimpanzee in hand to hand combat on even footing. I doubt it, though; the chimp would still bite your face off, and then would technically be ghouled but not blood bound in the process. Sucks to be you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}